 \\chi(D)=\\chi(0)+\\deg_k D$ silently carries finiteness content with no `Module.Finite` binder in sight. Both caveats now in the module docstring.", "created_at": "2026-07-27T17:04:53+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Adelic/BoundedVanishing.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 69, "del": 2, "loc_before": 538, "loc_after": 605, "loc_code_before": 298, "loc_code_after": 316, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"theorem": 16, "def": 1}, "decl_after": {"theorem": 17, "def": 1}, "decl_delta": {"theorem": 1}, "added": false, "deleted": false}], "lean": {"files": 1, "add": 69, "del": 2, "loc_after": 605, "loc_code_after": 316, "loc_delta": 67, "loc_code_delta": 18, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {"theorem": 17, "def": 1}, "decl_delta": {"theorem": 1}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 0}, {"sha": "31ee79aa1ae7945f97448dcf7983fc5b5b3111e8", "short_sha": "31ee79aa1a", "subject": "P-cluster: Riemann-Roch as an equality in the vanishing range", "summary": "`exists_bound_ell_eq`: there is a threshold $b$ past which $\\ell(D)=\\chi(0)+\\deg_k D$ \u2014 a FORMULA, not the inequality. Composes the vanishing bound with `ell_eq_of_bound`. With $\\chi(0)=1-g$ this is the classical $\\ell(D)=\\deg D+1-g$ for large degree.\n\nThis is the single statement a downstream rank-counting or Grassmannian-embedding consumer should quote: `degK_add_chi_zero_le_ell` gives the Riemann inequality always, and above $b$ it is an equality. Conditional on the same three inputs as the bound, and single-field.", "created_at": "2026-07-27T16:35:34+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJa